% One Hebrew word only: XeTeX lays out a maqaf- or space-joined Hebrew phrase as
% separate RTL runs in LTR order (word order and maqaf come out scrambled).
{\fontsize{15}{18}\selectfont\itshape\color{ChapterStone} זָכַר }\quad
{\footnotesize\scshape\color{CommentaryBrown} “zakar”}\quad
{\footnotesize\bfseries\color{ReturnAmber!80!black} 記念 \textperiodcentered\ 全書九次（尼 1:8; 13:31）}

\vfill

\fcolorbox{ScriptureGold}{white}{%
\begin{minipage}{4.3in}
\centering\vspace{0.15cm}
{\footnotesize\color{ReturnAmber!70!black}\kaiti\selectfont
「我又派百姓按定期獻柴和初熟的土產。\\我的神啊，求你記念我，施恩與我。」}\\[0.10em]
{\scriptsize\itshape\color{TextGray}
“and I arranged for the supply of wood at appointed times and for the first fruits.
Remember me, O my God, for good.”}\\[0.10em]
{\scriptsize\color{ChapterStone} 尼希米記 13:31 \textperiodcentered\ Nehemiah 13:31}
\vspace{0.15cm}
